  "notes": "{転換|てんかん} refers to a significant change or shift in direction, approach, or state.\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {気分|きぶん}{転換|てんかん} (change of mood/pace)\n- {方向|ほうこう}{転換|てんかん} (change of direction)\n- {路線|ろせん}{転換|てんかん} (change of course/policy)\n- {配置|はいち}{転換|てんかん} (reassignment, redeployment)\n- {転換|てんかん}{点|てん} (turning point)\n- {発想|はっそう}の{転換|てんかん} (shift in thinking)\n\nUSAGE:\n- Often used with する as a suru verb: {転換|てんかん}する (to convert, to shift)\n- Implies a deliberate or significant change, not a minor adjustment\n- {気分|きぶん}{転換|てんかん} is one of the most common everyday uses",
